      "content": "Valid economic arguments regarding grid stability and mineral shortages remain absolutely legitimate and will dominate operational risk for decades, even if the end goal of decarbonization is fixed. The debate is no longer about \"whether\" renewables will replace fossil fuels, but rather \"how,\" \"when,\" and \"what happens to those who fail to adapt.\" Therefore, treating energy assets as purely binary—either fully green or fully fossil-fuel—ignores the complex reality that the most valuable opportunities likely lie in the hybrid transition and the decarbonization of traditional energy assets, not in sticking blindly to pure old energy or the renewable ideal. The \"obligation to bet\" is simply the obligation to figure out how to cut your losses or find value within the transition, not to defend a dying business model.",
      "source": "target",
